What settled it: `acceptance-criteria.sh` already *reports rather than fails* a §13 criterion whose script doesn't exist yet, with a comment saying exactly why — failing would deadlock the run on its own definition of done before the first feature merges. Landing a red S1 now would recreate that deadlock by hand, and writing S1 now would also force the CLI syntax OD-1 deliberately left to the planner. The decision cites the vision's durable-evidence ruling, read as binding each observer to the change it can actually observe; the "not a follow-up, and not optional" clause was weighed as the statement against, and the decision records why it doesn't forbid the split. OD-4 amends only OD-1's allocation sentence; R1000 itself and its fixture values are untouched, so nothing is superseded.

